@startuml ECG Classification Pipeline Activity Diagram

' Title and skin parameters
title ECG Classification Pipeline\nFrom MIT-BIH Data Gathering to Deployment
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam swimlaneWidth 200
skinparam activityBackgroundColor #E8F4FC
skinparam activityBorderColor #1E88E5
skinparam activityStartColor #4CAF50
skinparam activityEndColor #F44336

|Data Gathering|
start
:Load MIT-BIH Arrhythmia Database;
note right
  48 records from 
  PhysioNet database
  Sampling rate: 360 Hz
end note

:Parse ECG signals (MLII lead);

:Load annotation files;
note right
  R-peak locations
  Beat type labels
  (N, V, A, L, R, etc.)
end note

|Data Modification|
:Apply Pan-Tompkins R-peak detection;

:Extract beats around R-peaks;
note right
  200 samples per beat
  (90 pre-R + 110 post-R)
end note

:Skip Record 119;
note right #FFCCCC
  **Record 119 completely excluded**
  Reserved for live testing
  and deployment validation
  (47 records used for training)
end note

:Create 7-beat context windows;
note right
  3 previous + 1 center + 3 subsequent
  Shape: (7, 200)
end note

:Apply binary labeling;
note right
  N = Normal (0)
  Others = Abnormal (1)
end note

:Record-wise train/val/test split;
note right
  70% train / 15% val / 15% test
  **No patient leakage**
end note

:Normalize with StandardScaler;
note right
  Fitted on training data ONLY
end note

|AI Modeling|
:Build Context-Aware CNN1D Model (v6);
note right
  Input: (batch, 7, 200)
  7 beats as channels
  1D convolutions
end note

:Train with class weights;
note right
  Handle imbalanced classes
  Use CrossEntropyLoss
end note

:Validate on held-out records;

:Evaluate on test records;

:Export model to ONNX format;
note right
  context_ecg_model.onnx
  context_ecg_scaler.pkl
end note

|Result / Deployment|
:Deploy realtime_frontend.py;
note right
  Flask web application
  Real-time ECG visualization
end note

:Load Record 119 for testing;
note right #CCFFCC
  **True unseen validation**
  This record was never used
  during training or validation
end note

:Real-time beat classification;
note right
  7-beat rolling buffer
  ONNX Runtime inference
end note

:Display results with accuracy;

:Export complete ECG to PNG/JPEG;
note right
  From 0 second to current
  realtime position
end note

stop

@enduml
